.TH COMIC\-IDENTIFY 1 "" "comic-identify @VERSION@"
.SH NAME
comic\-identify \- identify a comic from its cover and manage a digital comic collection
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B comic\-identify
.br
.B comic\-identify
.I cover
.br
.B comic\-identify buscar
.I title
.RI [ number ]
.br
.B comic\-identify
.RB { \-V | \-\-version }
.br
.B comic\-identify
.RB { \-h | \-\-help }
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B comic\-identify
is a GTK application to manage a collection of digital comics. It identifies a comic
by its cover or title (Grand Comics Database, Universo Marvel, Tebeosfera, barcode,
ComicVine and visual cover comparison), normalizes file names, writes
.I ComicInfo.xml
metadata, exports to GCstar, makes backups and offers an optional AI assistant that
uses the user's own session.
.PP
Without arguments it opens the graphical interface. Text commands never open a window.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B comic\-identify
Open the application.
.TP
.BI comic\-identify " cover"
Open the application with that cover loaded.
.I cover
can be an image file or a CBR or CBZ comic file.
.TP
.BI "comic\-identify buscar " title " [" number ]
Search the local Grand Comics Database index and print one result per line as
.IR "title | subtitle | URL" .
Print
.B Sin resultados.
if nothing matches. It does not open the interface. The index must have been imported
beforehand from the application settings (\(lqImportar volcado de GCD\(rq).
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a short usage message and exit.
.PP
Any other argument is rejected with a usage message and exit status 2; it never opens
the interface.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
.B buscar
found no Grand Comics Database index.
.TP
.B 2
Unknown command or missing argument.
.SH FILES
Files are kept under the XDG directories, in a
.I comic\-identify
subdirectory.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/comic\-identify/config.json
User settings (ComicVine key and collection folders). Defaults to
.IR ~/.config .
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/comic\-identify/
Local indexes (\fIgcd_es.db\fR, \fIuniversomarvel.db\fR, \fItebeosfera.db\fR,
\fIlibrary.db\fR), logs (\fIrenames.log\fR, \fImetadata.log\fR, \fIgcstar.log\fR)
and the user's own logos in \fIlogos/\fR. Defaults to
.IR ~/.local/share .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Base directory for the configuration file.
.TP
.B XDG_DATA_HOME
Base directory for indexes, logs and logos.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR 7z (1),
.BR unrar (1),
.BR zbarimg (1)
.PP
Project page: https://github.com/seguidodoblado/comic\-identify
